{
  "id": "blood_sugar_units",
  "title": "Blood Sugar Units",
  "description": "Convert between blood sugar units (mmol/L and mg/dL)",
  "type": "datatable",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "mmol/L",
        "mg/dL"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          3.9,
          70
        ],
        [
          4,
          72
        ],
        [
          5,
          90
        ],
        [
          6,
          108
        ],
        [
          7,
          126
        ],
        [
          7.1,
          128
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "content": "## Blood Sugar Unit Conversion",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "mmol_l",
          "label": "Blood Sugar (mmol/L)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 5.5,
          "unit": "mmol/L"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "mg_dl",
          "label": "Blood Sugar (mg/dL)",
          "formula": "inputs.mmol_l * 18",
          "unit": "mg/dL",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "content": "## Reverse Conversion",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "mg_dl_input",
          "label": "Blood Sugar (mg/dL)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 100,
          "unit": "mg/dL"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "mmol_l_output",
          "label": "Blood Sugar (mmol/L)",
          "formula": "inputs.mg_dl_input / 18",
          "unit": "mmol/L",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Reference Information\n\n**Conversion Factors:**\n- 1 mmol/L = 18 mg/dL\n- 1 mg/dL = mmol/L ÷ 18\n\n**Normal Blood Glucose Levels:**\n- Range: 3.9 to 7.1 mmol/L (70 to 130 mg/dL)\n- These are reference values for healthy individuals"
    }
  ]
}